INSERT INTO feature VALUES('sized-types','recursion','Sized types',NULL,'partial','notable',NULL,'A staged type is a classifier a type parameter instantiates at, read off the first later variable argument that holds it, erased to its plain code on the wire and re-derived by the kernel at readmission; a size and a map through map at the children''s stage check and readmit on the direct rose tree, the forged claim refuses StageNotBelow; the staged fixpoint stuck past its first position carries its leading arguments, gating at its staged argument in both engines; the size and the map over the direct rose tree run, passing `map` the children''s type as a code. PR 2 owes a stage on a signature (the explicit bounded annotation), the successor and infinity, the consistency gate, measures, and what the erasure cannot re-derive: a nested staged code, a non-variable argument, a callee result stage, a helper parameter at the plain domain. An explicit stage binder is an implicit in the prefix block (def f [i : Size] (x : Nat[<i])), bounded [i : Size, i < n], written at the call f[.i = s] or solved from every argument that shows it at the least stage the readings allow (from below, from above under a function argument''s domain, exactly inside a data type''s argument), two readings no stage satisfies refused StagesDisagree by name in both engines; a bounded binder read off an argument is checked against its bound at the call in both engines, refused StageNotBelow. A stage supplied by name at a call, f[.i = j], is held by the checker to the stage the arguments solve, a disagreement refused StagesDisagree at the call''s head; the supply rides the declaration and its content key, and the kernel re-derives every stage without it.','core-checker kernel-core','corpus/model/data/rose.gandr corpus/model/data/sized-higher-order.gandr corpus/pathological/data/rose.gandr corpus/pathological/data/sized-higher-order.gandr corpus/model/identity/int-accumulated.gandr corpus/model/data/followin